The open idea status is read from the idea schema, the first entry of its `status` enum: a
project overlay renaming it to `raw` makes the `raw` idea open and an `open` one not.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/_schemas/idea.yaml --
doc: idea

rules:
  - select: FRONTMATTER
    has:
      type: idea
      status: { enum: [raw, done] }
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/idea/0001-raw.md --
---
type: idea
title: A raw idea
created_at: 2026-10-10
status: raw
reviewed: 2026-10-11
---

## Idea

Raw.
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/idea/0002-open.md --
---
type: idea
title: An idea in the shipped open status
created_at: 2026-10-10
status: open
reviewed: 2026-10-11
---

## Idea

Open by the shipped schema, not by this one.
-- cmd --
booping status ideas
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
## ideas

| ref | title | created_at |
| --- | --- | --- |
| idea/0001 | A raw idea | 2026-10-10 |
